WEBVTT

00:01.780 --> 00:04.800
Fall, when skies are clear 
and horses grow stout.

00:05.870 --> 00:08.420
I still feel like I'm on summer break.

00:08.420 --> 00:10.640
The academy festival is approaching.

00:10.640 --> 00:14.100
It's understandable that 
you'd feel restless.

00:15.000 --> 00:17.710
<i>The academy festival of the hyumans' 
greatest academy city, Rotsgard,</i>

00:17.710 --> 00:19.030
<i>is as impressive as you'd expect.</i>

00:19.030 --> 00:23.960
<i>People gather from all over, 
and every shop is filled to capacity.</i>

00:24.400 --> 00:26.640
<i>Lasting an entire week,</i>

00:26.640 --> 00:29.610
<i>it's an event that livens up 
the city like no other.</i>

00:29.610 --> 00:30.910
I'm surprised.

00:31.310 --> 00:33.770
I didn't know a competitive 
tournament was involved, too.

00:33.770 --> 00:36.140
Your students are rather excited about it.

00:36.550 --> 00:39.650
Guests are invited from Limia and Gritonia

00:39.650 --> 00:44.370
to evaluate the next generation's 
talent through diplomatic conferences.

00:45.780 --> 00:49.510
So it's like a job-hunting 
fair for the students.

00:50.260 --> 00:52.270
I hope nothing bad happens.

01:12.170 --> 01:14.070
<b>Season Two</b>

02:24.990 --> 02:27.450
<b>Kuzunoha</b>

02:25.080 --> 02:29.000
<b>Night Thirteen   The Very Busy Academy Festival</b>

02:25.080 --> 02:29.000
<b>Night Thirteen   The Very Busy Academy Festival</b>

02:28.110 --> 02:29.390
Young Master.

02:30.420 --> 02:34.240
I'd like to discuss our inventory 
for the duration of the festival.

02:34.240 --> 02:36.460
The list of additional items 
should arrive tonight.

02:36.860 --> 02:38.460
We can decide after that.

02:38.460 --> 02:40.120
Makoto-kun!

02:40.120 --> 02:43.020
Let's check out the festival together.

02:43.020 --> 02:44.940
Tomoe and Mio will be coming that day.

02:45.310 --> 02:47.170
Why don't you go with them?

02:47.170 --> 02:49.610
You're no fun.

02:49.610 --> 02:51.100
Don't sit up there.

02:51.100 --> 02:53.580
Regarding additional staff for the store...

02:53.580 --> 02:56.510
The Elder Dwarves would 
probably be a good fit.

02:56.510 --> 02:59.620
You truly are kind to demihumans.

02:59.620 --> 03:02.360
Or do you just hate hyumans?

03:02.360 --> 03:06.960
Luto, let me be blunt...

03:06.960 --> 03:08.880
Get out of here.

03:09.210 --> 03:12.680
Whoops. Looks like I'm actually intruding.

03:12.680 --> 03:15.040
Guess I'll go do some work at the guild.

03:16.150 --> 03:18.980
Luto-dono never changes, does he?

03:18.980 --> 03:21.760
I'm shocked he of all 
people is the guildmaster.

03:22.470 --> 03:25.510
He'll be meeting important 
people at the festival.

03:25.510 --> 03:28.220
He said he uses the name "False" with them.

03:28.220 --> 03:33.140
I hear he once conducted rather 
intriguing experiments.

03:33.140 --> 03:35.870
I'd like to know more about his research.

03:36.890 --> 03:38.240
I thought you left...

03:40.710 --> 03:43.400
Thank you for meeting me 
on such short notice.

03:44.430 --> 03:49.370
My name is Shinai. I am a temple priest.

03:51.070 --> 03:53.760
<i>I'm Kuzunoha, the owner of this shop.</i>

03:53.760 --> 03:56.170
<i>Forgive my inability to speak.</i>

03:56.450 --> 03:57.880
Is it a curse?

03:57.880 --> 04:01.720
<i>Yes. I see it as a type of chronic condition.</i>

04:02.250 --> 04:03.570
I'm sorry to hear that.

04:03.570 --> 04:05.730
<i>Anyway, how can I help you today?</i>

04:06.010 --> 04:10.120
Right. It's regarding the medicines 
you carry at this store.

04:10.120 --> 04:14.610
Some people are concerned that 
they're too effective for their price.

04:14.980 --> 04:17.930
<i>I'm glad it's not about the goddess.</i>

04:18.370 --> 04:21.190
<i>Is he hoping for a bribe?</i>

04:21.570 --> 04:24.410
I thought such nonsensical rumors 
would be a bother to you.

04:24.410 --> 04:26.390
So I have a suggestion.

04:26.390 --> 04:28.950
<i>Definitely hoping for a bribe.</i>

04:28.950 --> 04:32.000
<i>If a few gold coins will shut 
them up, I'm willing to pay.</i>

04:32.000 --> 04:34.410
Have you considered allowing 
temples to handle sales?

04:34.410 --> 04:35.120
<i>What?</i>

04:35.120 --> 04:37.380
<i>I'm not sure I understand.</i>

04:37.380 --> 04:39.580
Then forget I said anything.

04:40.140 --> 04:43.560
The temple will assist in 
clearing up any rumors.

04:43.960 --> 04:46.310
However, we have a condition.

04:46.870 --> 04:47.960
<i>Let's hear it.</i>

04:48.330 --> 04:50.670
We want you to reveal your 
production methods.

04:52.680 --> 04:55.470
So the temple can inspect them, of course.

04:55.470 --> 04:58.060
We swear not to leak the 
information to other shops.

04:58.060 --> 05:03.150
<i>But if I revealed my methods, 
couldn't the temple produce similar products?</i>

05:04.280 --> 05:06.620
On that matter, we request 
your understanding.

05:07.560 --> 05:11.330
I believe I'm making a sound suggestion.

05:11.640 --> 05:15.780
<i>Several members of the temple were 
involved in those humanoid experiments.</i>

05:16.870 --> 05:19.030
<i>The previous bishop was one of them.</i>

05:19.340 --> 05:23.510
<i>He suddenly died an unnatural death, 
probably at Rona-san's hands.</i>

05:26.580 --> 05:31.550
<i>It couldn't hurt to have connections to 
the temple in case the unexpected occurs.</i>

05:32.480 --> 05:35.270
<i>I'm just a fledgling merchant.</i>

05:35.270 --> 05:38.070
<i>If it means getting to 
know people in the temple,</i>

05:38.070 --> 05:41.060
<i>I'll gladly disclose my production methods.</i>

05:41.060 --> 05:43.020
Y-You're sure?

05:43.670 --> 05:46.460
<i>Let me know what day is 
most convenient for you.</i>

05:46.460 --> 05:49.400
<i>I'll have my alchemist show 
you how they're made.</i>

05:49.770 --> 05:50.790
I appreciate it.

05:50.790 --> 05:52.670
Then come to the temple tomorrow at noon.

05:53.880 --> 05:55.130
Yikes.

05:55.130 --> 05:57.030
Is something the matter?

05:57.030 --> 06:00.090
It's quite the majestic building 
for worshiping that goddess.

06:00.450 --> 06:04.280
Worshipers see her as the one 
and only noble and good goddess

06:04.280 --> 06:09.650
who loves all hyumans like 
a pure mother, right?

06:09.650 --> 06:12.050
More or less, yes.

06:12.390 --> 06:15.020
<i>That's a pure mother?</i>

06:17.370 --> 06:20.940
<i>I don't think I'm going to get 
along with the temple's people.</i>

06:21.480 --> 06:23.050
Regarding this proposal,

06:23.050 --> 06:26.060
we appreciate the deep devotion 
you're demonstrating.

06:26.060 --> 06:31.020
The temple swears to clear up all rumors 
and lies concerning your store.

06:31.430 --> 06:33.240
<i>Thank you for your kindness.</i>

06:33.240 --> 06:36.960
I hear a chronic condition 
has rendered you mute.

06:36.960 --> 06:39.900
We shall devise a solution 
to that problem, too,

06:39.900 --> 06:42.990
though I'm not sure how much 
we'll be able to help.

06:42.990 --> 06:45.490
Your Holiness, it's time.

06:45.490 --> 06:47.860
We'll meet again.

07:00.660 --> 07:01.970
<i>Crap!</i>

07:02.580 --> 07:04.890
I'm disappointed, Kuzunoha-dono.

07:06.220 --> 07:09.440
You owe the bishop your utmost respect.

07:09.440 --> 07:11.570
<i>Forgive my poor manners.</i>

07:11.570 --> 07:14.660
No matter. So, how do you 
make your medicines?

07:14.660 --> 07:15.330
<i>Right.</i>

07:15.330 --> 07:16.630
<i>It's all in here.</i>

07:18.150 --> 07:24.620
I see. While the alchemists are working, 
I'd like you to tell us a few things.

07:24.620 --> 07:25.070
<i>Huh?</i>

07:28.020 --> 07:31.060
Oh, it's merely small talk.

07:34.340 --> 07:35.470
Kuzunoha-dono.

07:35.470 --> 07:36.020
<i>Yes?</i>

07:36.630 --> 07:39.380
How long have you been a merchant?

07:39.380 --> 07:41.230
<i>Fewer than three years.</i>

07:41.230 --> 07:44.720
<i>Whether it's been three days or two 
years, it's all less than three years.</i>

07:45.240 --> 07:48.020
And you have shops in two cities?

07:48.020 --> 07:49.930
Do you have a major backer?

07:50.250 --> 07:56.400
<i>Not a backer, but the Rembrandt Trading 
Company of Tsige has been kind to us.</i>

07:56.790 --> 07:58.880
Rembrandt? I see.

07:58.880 --> 08:00.700
<i>You know him?</i>

08:00.700 --> 08:06.740
<i>Not only did he lend me a storefront, 
but he also taught me the basics of business.</i>

08:07.310 --> 08:11.640
That's rather different from 
the Rembrandt we know.

08:12.290 --> 08:16.080
We'd appreciate it if he were 
a little more cooperative.

08:16.690 --> 08:18.590
<i>Oh, right.</i>

08:19.060 --> 08:24.600
<i>Rembrandt stopped worshiping the goddess 
after that business with the disease.</i>

08:24.930 --> 08:31.430
Do you look after his daughters at the 
academy because of your connection to him?

08:31.430 --> 08:33.780
<i>Huh? Am I being investigated?</i>

08:33.780 --> 08:38.120
<i>Yes. I've been asked to 
keep an eye out for them.</i>

08:38.120 --> 08:40.730
He loves his daughters dearly.

08:41.420 --> 08:44.610
Perhaps I should reevaluate 
my impression of him.

08:47.260 --> 08:49.090
Did Kuzunoha and his man leave?

08:49.090 --> 08:51.800
Yes. They just exited the temple.

08:53.460 --> 08:56.280
We're having him followed.

08:56.980 --> 08:59.110
You wasted our time.

08:59.560 --> 09:03.720
In the future, get my approval first 
on all matters concerning him.

09:03.720 --> 09:05.450
Wh-What do you mean?

09:05.830 --> 09:09.560
Our examinations of his 
mind and mana failed.

09:11.020 --> 09:13.310
He blocked all our attempts.

09:13.880 --> 09:16.840
A servant couldn't possibly tail him.

09:16.840 --> 09:19.610
His production methods were fishy, too.

09:19.860 --> 09:21.070
What?

09:21.400 --> 09:26.310
The steps and explanations were clear, 
and the methods themselves were marvelous.

09:26.310 --> 09:30.300
But with our abilities, we'd have 
only a 50% chance of success.

09:30.300 --> 09:31.660
Only 50%?

09:31.660 --> 09:34.500
Furthermore, when you consider 
the material and labor costs,

09:34.500 --> 09:37.300
we'd have to charge a hundred times the price.

09:37.750 --> 09:39.510
N-No...

09:39.510 --> 09:44.270
Kuzunoha is something else entirely 
pretending to be an innocent child.

09:45.090 --> 09:49.730
But it's also possible he'll become 
our trump card in the future.

09:49.730 --> 09:51.690
<b>Kuzunoha</b>

09:50.510 --> 09:51.690
What?!

09:52.050 --> 09:55.980
Eris-san, does that mean you 
can beat Mr. Blue Lizard?

09:55.980 --> 10:00.280
Of course. I couldn't work 
here if I couldn't manage that.

10:00.280 --> 10:03.770
That's amazing! Will you teach me some 
incantations in the old language, too?

10:03.370 --> 10:05.910
How long is Eris going to slack off?

10:03.770 --> 10:06.690
I'd also like to learn how to 
perform incantations while in motion.

10:05.910 --> 10:07.360
We're back.

10:06.690 --> 10:09.180
How do you do it while 
leaping around like that?

10:07.360 --> 10:09.480
W-Welcome back.

10:09.180 --> 10:11.780
Really? That's the most basic of basics.

10:09.480 --> 10:11.660
They look like they're having fun.

10:11.780 --> 10:13.820
It shouldn't need to be taught.

10:12.470 --> 10:14.760
When did they start getting along like that?

10:13.820 --> 10:15.530
Please! I beg you!

10:14.760 --> 10:17.120
J-Just now, actually.

10:17.120 --> 10:18.770
If you tell me the truth,

10:18.770 --> 10:23.130
I'll let you taste the banana milk we 
developed for the academy festival.

10:23.710 --> 10:25.320
Since two hours ago!

10:28.080 --> 10:31.590
The rich sweetness of the banana, 
light aroma of the syrup,

10:31.590 --> 10:35.000
and profound flavor of the chilled 
milk spread throughout my mouth.

10:36.100 --> 10:38.200
I wish I could drown in it.

10:38.200 --> 10:39.940
I'm glad you like it.

10:39.940 --> 10:44.550
The key is to choose magic words from 
the old language that suit you.

10:44.550 --> 10:47.610
Where did you fight Mr. Blue Lizard?

10:47.610 --> 10:50.420
I've never seen scales like his before.

10:50.780 --> 10:53.680
Of course not. After all, he's a Mist—

10:53.670 --> 10:57.130
<b>DANGLE</b>

10:54.550 --> 10:57.650
Sh-Shiki-sama, Young Master.

10:57.650 --> 11:00.080
You're being a bit too proud.

11:00.350 --> 11:05.060
<i>Eris, do you want to go back 
to the demiplane boot camp?</i>

11:07.010 --> 11:09.470
You planned this, Aqua!

11:10.120 --> 11:12.690
Young Master, Eris has 
turned over a new leaf.

11:12.690 --> 11:14.450
I'll never be so arrogant again.

11:14.450 --> 11:16.660
So please... please...

11:16.660 --> 11:19.910
Please have mercy on me!

11:20.420 --> 11:22.330
<i>The rest is up to you.</i>

11:22.330 --> 11:24.860
<i>I'm off to make deliveries.</i>

11:24.860 --> 11:25.880
Very well.

11:28.340 --> 11:29.710
<i>Also, Jin.</i>

11:29.710 --> 11:30.280
Yes?!

11:30.840 --> 11:35.510
<i>If you're going to cheat, 
don't bother coming to class anymore.</i>

11:36.140 --> 11:38.810
I-I'm very sorry.

11:40.470 --> 11:41.950
Got your goods all set up?

11:41.950 --> 11:43.840
Just about to.

11:43.840 --> 11:46.290
Better hurry. The festival's starting.

11:43.840 --> 11:48.310
<i>Fall days end quickly, 
but the crowds don't disperse.</i>

11:46.290 --> 11:48.290
I know, I know.

11:48.310 --> 11:50.570
Huh? I sense something...

11:54.270 --> 11:55.740
I'm being followed.

11:56.160 --> 11:59.740
That's not animosity, that's bloodlust.

12:00.740 --> 12:03.110
In that case, I'll pretend I haven't noticed.

12:12.710 --> 12:14.330
<i>They finally made their move.</i>

12:14.330 --> 12:17.730
<i>Judging by their outfits, 
they belong to the assassin's guild.</i>

12:19.290 --> 12:20.340
Get him!

12:22.530 --> 12:23.390
Brid.

12:34.260 --> 12:35.310
<i>He's...</i>

12:38.780 --> 12:42.020
<i>Here for revenge, 
assassin who's proud of his blade?</i>

12:42.020 --> 12:45.480
I always complete every job.

12:45.480 --> 12:48.500
<i>I can't decide if you're dutiful or obsessed.</i>

12:48.500 --> 12:50.450
<i>Hey, I see your blade's been fixed.</i>

12:52.100 --> 12:57.250
This blade made from the scales of Greater 
Dragon Mitsurugi is my pride itself.

12:57.250 --> 13:00.620
There is no greater assassin's 
blade in the world!

13:01.130 --> 13:03.380
<i>Mitsurugi? He's talking about Lancer.</i>

13:03.380 --> 13:06.800
<i>His scales are wasted on that blade.</i>

13:07.220 --> 13:09.530
<i>Well, he seemed like an unpleasant guy.</i>

13:09.530 --> 13:12.030
<i>Maybe his scales are just right 
for an assassin's weapon.</i>

13:12.030 --> 13:13.750
What's so funny?!

13:14.140 --> 13:20.030
Die, die, die!

13:15.950 --> 13:18.940
<i>Is this guy on some sketchy drugs?</i>

13:20.320 --> 13:21.900
<i>I should end this.</i>

13:28.350 --> 13:34.320
<i>Now, then... I'd like the assassin's 
guild to leave me alone, so...</i>

13:34.320 --> 13:39.220
<i>This will truly end the 
matter with Bright-sensei.</i>

13:51.290 --> 13:55.590
<i>I'm agitated. I need to 
find a way to calm down.</i>

14:01.410 --> 14:03.400
Welcome back, Young Master.

14:04.480 --> 14:07.370
I was just thinking about 
reaching out to you.

14:07.860 --> 14:08.950
I'm back, Tomoe.

14:09.580 --> 14:12.640
How's your investigation into 
the demiplane's climate going?

14:12.640 --> 14:16.570
We can wait to act until after 
the festival has ended, but...

14:20.610 --> 14:24.220
I believe I've found a 
rather effective method.

14:24.490 --> 14:29.190
Opening a mist gate here would produce 
a climate that's a 95% match for Japan's.

14:29.500 --> 14:31.390
The weather would stabilize.

14:31.390 --> 14:33.110
But this place is...

14:33.110 --> 14:36.750
Yes. It's controlled by demons.

14:38.350 --> 14:41.540
They have a fortress nearby.

14:41.540 --> 14:44.890
It would be a bad idea to leave traces 
of activity right before their eyes.

14:44.890 --> 14:46.520
Then what should we do?

14:46.520 --> 14:50.160
With your permission, I could 
clean up the area right away.

14:51.830 --> 14:57.860
<i>Attacking the fortress would earn the 
demons' hostility, and this place...</i>

14:59.460 --> 15:01.320
Let me think about it.

15:01.320 --> 15:06.310
Very well. For now, let's enjoy 
the festival that starts tomorrow.

15:07.480 --> 15:08.950
Great deals here!

15:08.950 --> 15:10.950
We've got stuff you can use 
to cheer on the competitors!

15:10.950 --> 15:12.880
All the stalls look amazing!

15:11.870 --> 15:13.240
That looks tasty!

15:13.240 --> 15:14.860
That's the academy city for you.

15:14.860 --> 15:16.780
Let's look over there, too.

15:17.230 --> 15:19.280
So this is the academy city.

15:19.280 --> 15:21.420
It's more vibrant than Tsige.

15:21.420 --> 15:23.790
All the shops look so tasty.

15:23.790 --> 15:25.930
Don't eat the whole festival 
while you're at it.

15:25.930 --> 15:27.190
What's the holdup?

15:27.190 --> 15:28.710
Wow, what a crowd.

15:28.710 --> 15:29.600
Hurry up!

15:29.600 --> 15:31.360
How long are you gonna make us wait?

15:29.980 --> 15:31.360
We traveled a long way for this!

15:31.920 --> 15:34.320
So noisy...

15:36.040 --> 15:37.870
Thank you.

15:38.470 --> 15:39.850
Good morning.

15:39.850 --> 15:42.050
<i>Sorry! I totally overslept!</i>

15:42.050 --> 15:46.090
You couldn't help it. You were 
up until dawn preparing for...

15:43.870 --> 15:45.130
How much for this?

15:44.490 --> 15:45.850
Got any of these in stock?

15:45.130 --> 15:47.230
I'm sorry. One moment, please.

15:45.850 --> 15:47.230
Could I get some of these?

15:47.230 --> 15:48.720
Yes. One moment, please.

15:48.720 --> 15:51.080
What does this medicine do?

15:49.920 --> 15:51.940
One moment, please!

15:51.940 --> 15:53.710
Our salesperson spirits burn!

15:54.210 --> 15:56.430
<i>Where are Lime and the new Elder Dwarf?</i>

15:56.430 --> 15:57.460
Outside.

15:57.930 --> 16:00.960
The end of the line is over here!

16:01.350 --> 16:04.490
We're currently restricting admission!

16:04.850 --> 16:08.760
I've asked them to organize the 
line to avoid bothering other shops.

16:08.760 --> 16:10.760
How are sales?

16:10.760 --> 16:13.260
We're nearly done for the day.

16:13.260 --> 16:14.180
That good?

16:14.180 --> 16:18.740
Adventurers who heard about us by word 
of mouth are visiting from across the land.

16:18.740 --> 16:23.470
I'm thinking of distributing numbered 
tickets or vouchers if we run out of stock.

16:23.470 --> 16:24.860
<i>Vouchers, huh?</i>

16:24.860 --> 16:27.700
<i>Come to think of it, 
the merchant's guild gave us some.</i>

16:27.990 --> 16:30.500
Forgive me for not seeking 
your permission first.

16:30.790 --> 16:34.330
I thought about waking you, but...

16:35.080 --> 16:37.170
The young master is tired.

16:37.170 --> 16:39.770
Why won't you let him rest?

16:39.770 --> 16:44.590
As his followers, we'd never 
disturb his restful sleep.

16:44.850 --> 16:47.380
Sorry. That must have been 
exhausting for you.

16:47.380 --> 16:48.260
Not at all.

16:48.260 --> 16:49.610
So, what are they up to?

16:50.570 --> 16:54.440
They went with Luto-dono 
to check out the food.

16:54.440 --> 16:59.340
I see. Once I'm done checking inventory, 
I'm going to make my rounds.

16:59.340 --> 17:00.200
I appreciate it.

17:00.720 --> 17:02.570
Let's see. First up is...

17:02.570 --> 17:03.660
Kuzuha...

17:06.020 --> 17:08.840
Why is it written in Laurel's secret script?

17:08.840 --> 17:10.010
Laurel?

17:10.010 --> 17:12.180
Please don't cut in line, sir.

17:12.180 --> 17:14.850
What? I'm not gonna listen to a demihuman.

17:14.850 --> 17:16.390
It's store rules.

17:16.390 --> 17:19.910
Seriously? Does this shop 
employ demihumans?

17:19.260 --> 17:21.550
<i>A hyuman scumbag.</i>

17:21.550 --> 17:23.100
<i>I'll ask him to leave.</i>

17:34.800 --> 17:40.160
Delicious. I hate myself for not 
bringing hot sake to drink.

17:40.160 --> 17:43.010
Fish, meat, vegetables, seasoning.

17:43.010 --> 17:45.760
And most of all, the soup that 
is the foundation of the dish.

17:45.760 --> 17:48.530
Now this is a dish worth learning to make.

17:48.870 --> 17:51.020
Aqua, let me have a taste already.

17:51.020 --> 17:53.550
Doesn't matter if they're 
demihuman or hyuman.

17:53.550 --> 17:54.930
I'll kick their asses.

17:54.930 --> 17:55.950
I appreciate it.

17:57.100 --> 17:58.410
Young Master.

17:59.500 --> 18:01.400
Cream and mayonnaise.

18:01.760 --> 18:04.470
What kind of harmony will they create?

18:04.470 --> 18:07.280
Shiki, no horrifying experiments, okay?

18:07.760 --> 18:09.280
Thank you for waiting.

18:09.280 --> 18:10.910
Here's the extra hotpot you ordered.

18:10.910 --> 18:14.230
<i>The restaurant is packed. Got enough staff?</i>

18:14.230 --> 18:17.990
We'll be fine. We're prepared for the rush.

18:18.380 --> 18:20.800
My sister's helping, too.

18:20.800 --> 18:24.400
<i>Eva-san can wait on customers, too? 
She has many talents.</i>

18:24.780 --> 18:29.590
Actually, she's washing 
dishes in the kitchen.

18:29.590 --> 18:32.420
Since I work here, she helps every year,

18:32.420 --> 18:37.260
but we all have our 
strengths and weaknesses.

18:37.260 --> 18:39.920
<i>So customer service isn't 
one of her strengths.</i>

18:39.920 --> 18:43.490
Let me know if you'd like anything else.

18:43.490 --> 18:44.490
<i>Thanks.</i>

18:44.490 --> 18:47.690
Young Master, what a truly 
delightful festival.

18:47.690 --> 18:50.670
I can see why it brings in foreign nobles.

18:50.670 --> 18:54.790
There's a great variety of stalls 
selling foods I've never seen before.

18:54.790 --> 18:59.100
In Laurel, they apparently eat fish raw.

18:59.100 --> 19:01.400
Really? They eat sashimi there, huh?

19:01.650 --> 19:04.770
Seeing the students train warmed my heart.

19:04.770 --> 19:08.410
I'm sure your own students will 
do their best at the tournament.

19:08.760 --> 19:11.050
Let's go watch the matches together.

19:11.050 --> 19:13.340
Enjoy the festival to your 
hearts' content, you two.

19:13.340 --> 19:15.070
Of course!

19:16.920 --> 19:19.340
I kind of feel like you're having <i>too</i> much fun.

19:23.140 --> 19:24.270
Now...

19:24.680 --> 19:28.280
What does Laurel want from Limia?

19:29.860 --> 19:31.810
Allow me to be direct.

19:32.570 --> 19:34.430
Please return our priestess to us.

19:36.360 --> 19:37.980
The priestess?

19:37.980 --> 19:44.580
She is with Hibiki-dono, the hero of Limia, 
and chose to accompany her into battle.

19:44.580 --> 19:49.640
Your great hyuman nation has kidnapped 
a key figure of another nation

19:49.640 --> 19:52.290
and is forcing her to participate 
in dangerous battles.

19:52.740 --> 19:55.370
This will become a serious issue.

19:56.570 --> 20:00.500
The priestess took the lead 
in supporting the hero.

20:00.500 --> 20:03.590
Shouldn't that make your nation proud?

20:04.340 --> 20:06.460
Does Limia take hostages?

20:06.460 --> 20:07.640
What?

20:07.640 --> 20:12.810
You know how important 
the priestess is to us.

20:12.810 --> 20:17.850
If you refuse to accept it, 
then send your own forces.

20:18.250 --> 20:21.230
We'll assign them to travel 
with the priestess.

20:24.670 --> 20:26.250
Leaving so soon?

20:27.630 --> 20:30.300
The priestess cannot be replaced.

20:30.300 --> 20:35.200
I hope we make some progress during 
our stay in the academy city.

20:36.030 --> 20:37.420
I'll keep that in mind.

20:42.800 --> 20:44.830
This is ridiculous.

20:44.830 --> 20:48.980
We're busy preparing a second 
attack against Fort Stella.

20:48.980 --> 20:54.220
If the empire hadn't sent the princess, 
we wouldn't have needed to come here.

20:55.390 --> 20:59.820
The empire's hero and Princess 
Lily are wholly to blame.

21:00.170 --> 21:03.240
What are those imperial bastards planning?

21:08.700 --> 21:11.280
Very good, very good!

21:10.850 --> 21:13.270
Please stop!

21:11.280 --> 21:13.880
I like you, Luria!

21:13.880 --> 21:16.790
Please forgive my sister for being so inept.

21:16.790 --> 21:19.620
Oil! I need more oil!

21:19.620 --> 21:22.250
The stuff that burns on the way down!

21:22.250 --> 21:24.770
This is my next new product.

21:24.770 --> 21:26.360
Is it banana and mayo?

21:26.360 --> 21:27.660
No, it's banana milk.

21:27.660 --> 21:29.850
Hotpot is delicious.

21:29.850 --> 21:31.920
Let's hit up a second bar, boss!

21:31.920 --> 21:34.460
Of course. How could we not?

21:34.460 --> 21:35.810
Banana milk!

21:39.700 --> 21:41.140
<i>Even when sober,</i>

21:41.140 --> 21:42.480
<i>I too feel enlivened by</i>

21:42.480 --> 21:43.740
<i>brisk autumn breezes.</i>

21:52.080 --> 21:54.810
What a bunch of fools.

21:54.810 --> 21:57.130
They're nothing like the empire's people.

23:34.950 --> 23:36.720
Night Fourteen:

23:35.560 --> 23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

23:36.720 --> 23:39.210
"I'm Not a Fan of High Society."

23:36.940 --> 23:40.020
<b>I'm Not a Fan of High Society</b>
